## Configuration
Stage 0 (feature OFF, 16:22–16:24; evidence/38408/38408-cfg-base.sh + .out). The same VLANs, trunks and
decoy as below, WITHOUT any `vlan-stacking` line:
```
SA:   vlan 3995 name ck-svlan; port1.0.13 mode trunk / trunk native vlan 3993 / trunk allowed vlan add 3995;
      port1.0.2 trunk allowed vlan add 3995
x230: vlan 3995; port1.0.3 mode trunk / native 3991 / allowed add 3995; port1.0.1 allowed add 3995
DUT:  vlan 3995 name ck-svlan, vlan 2100 name ck-cvlan-decoy
      port3.0.13 switchport access vlan 3995
      port1.0.13 mode trunk / trunk allowed vlan add 3995 / trunk native vlan 3993
      port1.0.2  mode trunk / trunk allowed vlan add 3995 / trunk native vlan 3991
      port1.0.9  switchport access vlan 2100
```
Two refusals came from my script, not the DUT: try 1 stopped on my show form `show vlan 3993-3995`
(`% ` after every SA config line had applied), and try 2 stopped on the re-sent `vlan 3995 name ck-svlan`
(`% VLAN 3995 is already named ck-svlan`). Try 3 skipped the SA part, which was already applied. Raw:
38408-cfg-base-try1.out, -try2.out, 38408-cfg-base.out.
Steps 1 + 2 (16:25:11–16:25:19; 38408-cfg-qinq.sh + .out, no `% ` line):
```
interface port3.0.13 / switchport vlan-stacking customer-edge-port
interface port1.0.13 / switchport vlan-stacking provider-port
interface port1.0.2  / switchport vlan-stacking provider-port
```
