## Traffic
Sender: evidence/vsend.py (scapy), 100 × IPv4/UDP per stage, unknown-unicast dst (flooded), marker
CKVLAN-<stage>-<seq>. Driver: evidence/group-2026-09-30/vstep.sh. Captures are `tcpdump -Q in -e -w`
filtered on the sender MAC, one per listed NIC, stopped by PID and counted by vcount.py (tags read
from the 802.1Q headers). DUT counters are `show interface … | include input|output packets`
before and after each burst. Background on these ports is about +11 to +34 per ~20 s read interval.

| stage | sent (NIC, tags on the wire) | captured | DUT deltas (in/out) | result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| s0f — feature OFF | eth1 → port3.0.13, 100 × `tags=2100` | eth2 **0**, eth3 **0** | 3.0.13 in +100; 1.0.13 out +23, 1.0.2 out +33 (background) | dropped: no QinQ, no forwarding (baseline) |
| s1f — step 1, CE ingress | eth1, 100 × `tags=2100` | eth2 **100 × `tags=3995,2100`**, eth3 **100 × `tags=3995,2100`**, decoy 0 | 3.0.13 in +100; 1.0.13 out +122, 1.0.2 out +134, 1.0.9 out +11 | **PASS**: outer 3995 added, customer tag kept, both provider ports |
| s1u — step 1, CE ingress untagged | eth1, 100 × untagged | eth2 **100 × `tags=3995`**, eth3 **100 × `tags=3995`** | 3.0.13 in +100; 1.0.13 out +123, 1.0.2 out +133 | **PASS**: outer added to an untagged customer frame |
| s1r — steps 1 + 2 | eth2 → SA → provider port1.0.13, 100 × `tags=3995,2100` | eth1 **100 × `tags=2100`**; eth3 **100 × `tags=3995,2100`**; no tag-3992 (decoy) frame at eth3 | 1.0.13 in +123; 3.0.13 out +122; 1.0.2 out +134; 1.0.9 out +12 (background) | **PASS**: CE egress removed the outer tag; provider → provider switched on 3995 and left still double-tagged; decoy VLAN 2100 got nothing |
| s2r — step 2, other provider port, other inner VID | eth3 → x230 → provider port1.0.2, 100 × `tags=3995,2200` | eth1 **100 × `tags=2200`**; eth2 **100 × `tags=3995,2200`**; eth3 inbound 0 | 1.0.2 in +101; 3.0.13 out +122; 1.0.13 out +122; 1.0.9 out +12 | **PASS**: switched on the outer tag whatever the inner VID; still double-tagged on the provider egress |

Raw: evidence/38408/38408-s{0f,1f,1u,1r,2r}.out and the per-NIC .pcap files.

Per the case's expected results:
- Step 1 "Traffic leaving this port will have the outer-tag removed. Traffic entering this port will
  have an outer-tag added": s1r/s2r (removed, 200/200) and s1f/s1u (added, 200/200). **PASS**.
- Step 2 "Double tagged traffic should be switched based on the outer-tag. Traffic leaving this port
  should still be double tagged": s1r/s2r (switched on 3995 to the S-VLAN's ports only, the decoy VLAN
  2100 received nothing, inner 2100 and 2200 handled the same) and provider egress still `3995,<inner>`
  (200/200). **PASS**.

